---
title: Birds
description: Measurement fields for specimens in an Ornithology catalog.
sidebar:
  order: 2
---

Specimens in a project that uses the `Ornithology` catalog format show the bird
measurement form. Sex, life stage, and weight units work the same way in every
taxon group; see [Measurements](/en/usages/specimens/measurements/).

## Measurements

- `Weight`: specimen weight in the selected unit.
- `Wingspan (mm)`: wingspan length.
- Soft-part colors: `Bill color`, `Maxilla color`, `Mandible color`,
  `Iris color`, `Tarsus color`, and `Toe color`.
- `Sex`: select from the configured specimen-sex vocabulary.
- `Life stage`: select from the configured life-stage vocabulary.
- `Brood patch`: whether a brood patch is present.
- `Bursa present`: whether a bursa is present. If present, record bursa length
  and width.
- `Skull ossification (%)`: selected from the available percentage list.
- `Fat`: fat category from `None` through `Extremely Heavy`.
- `Stomach contents`: notes on stomach contents.

## Gonads

- Male gonad fields: testis length, width, and remarks.
- Female gonad fields: ovary length, ovary width, ovary appearance, ova sizes,
  oviduct width, oviduct appearance, and remarks.

## Molt and notes

- Molt fields: wing molt, tail molt, body molt, and molt remarks.
- Notes: habitat remarks and specimen remarks.

## Parts and parasites

Bird catalogs show parasite-detection fields and the parasite tab. See
[Specimen Parts](/en/usages/specimens/parts/).
